This failure capsule retains all 18 non-source artifact files, including raw output, composition/acquisition receipts and both observation files, plus the job log and local backup attestation. Its **354 omitted `verification/source/` snapshot payloads** remain in the complete, byte-verified 372-file readable local backup. Their identities and source manifests remain public. Source stability and the failed test outcome are separate recorded facts; the full Archive and ten-application suites remain open.

[The earlier attempt38808025295](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-prerequisites-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) ran on the composed overlay based on `b15d166`: **161 checks, 155 passes, six failures and zero skips**, with a stable 779-file census. Its path-spelling diagnostic records `differentSpelling=true` for the hosted short-name temporary path and its long-name form. This failed epoch remains preserved separately from the later literal-path correction.

That capsule preserves all 32 non-source artifact files, including every prerequisite receipt and acquisition log, the candidate raw output and both observations, plus the job log and backup attestation. Its **357 omitted source-snapshot payloads** remain in the complete, verified 389-file local backup. Their identities and manifests remain public. Its prerequisite phases passed separately from its failed candidate result.

[The later attempt38808918976](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-aes-finite-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **161/161 finite experimental checks**, with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos, after the literal-path correction. Its actual tested Git baseline is merge `7d5bde3fb94e3383e6d85e50e7d567516cc6202c` at `refs/pull/1/merge`; PR head `aeb62e6` is a separate identity. The composition manifest SHA256 is `4fe7b114341199fa31d5553ffb3505db0e3427337ea8c72c637a8d5a3501a042`. The 779-file composed census remained stable, and the separate post-run source check passed. All three ZIP, plain-7Z and encrypted-7Z path diagnostics retain `differentSpelling=true`, showing `RUNNER~1` paths resolving to `runneradmin` paths while the physical timestamp checks pass.

The successful finite capsule preserves all **32 non-source artifact files**, including metadata, prerequisite receipts and logs, raw test output and both observations, plus the job log, local backup attestation and preservation collector. Its **357 source-snapshot payloads** are explicitly omitted publicly and remain in the complete, byte-verified **389-file** readable local backup. Their exact paths, sizes and digests remain in the public omission list and source manifests. Finite experimental contracts pass; production installation remains false, and browser acceptance, the full Archive scope and the full ten-application suite remain pending.

`compose-archive-aes-cloud.mjs` authenticates the committed baseline and selected experimental source bytes, then composes an explicit overlay in the ephemeral hosted checkout. The changes include selected AES/container behavior and source timestamp collection. `composition.json` records the baseline Git commit, approved source identities and the composed source census; the test collector receives it through `--overlay-manifest`. Each tested source identity combines its actual baseline commit and composition manifest. A stable before/after census describes that attempt's composed bytes and does not equate them with the Git baseline. The composition is confined to the experimental hosted checkout; production installation remains false.

